From ddc7765640013ddee565f204db3edbe3ba4a8667 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 20:41:49 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] U04: essay first sentence on a phone's first screen, and
 Crossway's ESV notice

The essay page (ArticleDetail) now reaches the essay's first sentence on a
390 x 844 phone screen instead of about 1,600px down:

- No art between the header and the text. Generated art is no longer drawn
  on the essay page; a real cover, where one exists, sits after the opening
  section (before the first "## " heading), lazy-loaded and not printed.
- The "In this essay" contents card starts closed at 760px and below, open
  above it; the reader can still open it.
- The reading tools (Listen, A- A+, Focus) sit in one row on a phone: the
  visible "Text size" word is hidden at 480px and below and stays the
  group's accessible name (TextSize gains a .text-size__label hook).
- A 16px gutter and tighter spacing on phones, through .essay-* classes in
  index.css; desktop spacing is unchanged. An essay that opens on a section
  heading starts at the top of the column.

Crossway's notice (lib/esv.ts, ESV_NOTICE) follows the body of an essay
that quotes the ESV, and prints with it. A rewrite (client/public/essays,
held to the ESV by the house rule) carries it once it quotes Scripture
with a reference; an older database essay carries it only where its own
text names the ESV, since those essays mix translations without naming
them. The notice wording was read through search results for
crossway.org/permissions (the site is unreachable from the sandbox) and
is waiting for James to confirm it against the page.

